{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/tasks.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Tasks: skill-decomposition\n\n## Feature Tasks\n\n- [x] 1. Move mission skill, mission-resume, and mission-status\n  Move `.claude/skills/mission/` (SKILL.md + templates/ + prompts/) to `skills/mission/`. Move `.claude/skills/mission-resume/` to `skills/mission-resume/`. Move `.claude/skills/mission-status/` to `skills/mission-status/`. Do not change any skill content in any of these three.\n\n- [x] 1a. Update mission SKILL.md skill references\n  In `skills/mission/SKILL.md`, replace all occurrences of old skill invocation names with new ones: `/grill-me` → `/grill`, `/write-a-prd` → `/prd`, `/ubiquitous-language` → `/language`, `/darkfactory-init` → `/mission-init`. No other content changes. This implements PRD user story 10 and was added during the coverage audit.\n\n- [x] 2. Fork grill, language, and prd skills\n  Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/grill-me/SKILL.md` to `skills/grill/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `grill`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/ubiquitous-language/SKILL.md` to `skills/language/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `language`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/write-a-prd/SKILL.md` to `skills/prd/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `prd`. Content otherwise unchanged.\n\n- [x] 3. Fork tdd and test-quality skills\n  Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/tdd/SKILL.md` and all 5 companion files (`deep-modules.md`, `interface-design.md`, `mocking.md`, `refactoring.md`, `tests.md`) to `skills/tdd/`, update frontmatter name to `tdd`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/test-quality-review/SKILL.md` to `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `test-quality`. Also update the one reference in `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md`: replace `/test-quality-review` with `/test-quality` in check 14.\n\n- [x] 4. Fork security skill\n  Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/security-review/SKILL.md` to `skills/security/SKILL.md`. Update frontmatter name to `security`. Remove any toyo-review-specific sections (references to toyo's review conventions or toyo-specific severity levels). Preserve all general security review logic.\n\n- [x] 5. Write mission-init skill\n  Write `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md`. This replaces `darkfactory-init` with symlink-based verification. The skill checks that each of the 12 skills has a symlink at `~/.claude/skills/<name>` pointing to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>`. On missing or broken symlinks it suggests running `install.sh`. Retains: CLI tool checks (codex, darkfactory-dispatch, gh, openspec, jq), coverage tool detection per project language (Rust/TypeScript/Python), and `openspec init --tools claude,codex --force` if `openspec/config.yaml` is absent.\n\n- [x] 6. Write adversarial skill\n  Write `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md`. Standalone dual-agent review skill: dispatches a Codex reviewer via `darkfactory-dispatch --async`, then launches a Claude reviewer via the Agent tool. Both receive identical input (current diff by default; PR diff via `gh pr diff <number>` if a PR number is given; a specific file if a path is given). Reports written to `mission/validations/adversarial-codex.md` and `adversarial-claude.md` (or temp paths outside a mission). After both complete, surfaces disagreements between the two reports.\n\n- [x] 7. Write dispatch skill\n  Write `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md`. Thin user-facing wrapper around the `darkfactory-dispatch` binary. Accepts a task description inline or prompts for one. Calls `darkfactory-dispatch` with a prompt file and `--json`, parses the structured result, and presents outcome (status, duration, files written, output path). Reports failure clearly; does not suppress it.\n\n- [x] 8. Create install.sh\n  Write `install.sh` at the repo root. POSIX-portable (`#!/bin/sh`), loops over `skills/*/` directories, creates `ln -sf` symlinks from `~/.claude/skills/<name>` to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each. Idempotent. Prints one line per skill and a final count. Make the file executable.\n\n- [x] 9. Update README.md and UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n  Rewrite three README sections: (1) First-time install — replace the block of manual `ln -sf` commands with `git clone` + `~/.darkfactory/install.sh`. (2) Skills table — replace the 4-row legacy table with the full 12-skill table. (3) Required external skills section — skills previously listed as external (`grill-me`, `ubiquitous-language`, `write-a-prd`, `tdd`, `test-quality-review`, `security-review`) are now bundled; remove them from the external table, keep only `/review` and `/simplify` (built-in Claude Code) and `/test-app` and `/demo-video` (optional project-specific). Update UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md: change \"separate skill\" to \"owned skill\" in the test-quality term definition.\n\n## Closing Tasks\n\n- [ ] C1. Smoke test\n  Run `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` and verify: (1) all 12 symlinks exist under `~/.claude/skills/` and resolve to the correct `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` targets; (2) running `/mission-init` in a project with a `Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, or `pyproject.toml` reports the expected coverage tool status.\n\n- [ ] C2. Cleanup\n  Remove any dead code, leftover scaffold, or draft files introduced during the mission. Check that no skill file contains references to old names (`grill-me`, `write-a-prd`, `ubiquitous-language`, `darkfactory-init`, `test-quality-review`). Verify no skill references the external `~/.darkfactory-skills/` repo path.\n\n- [ ] C3. Module shape re-check\n  Audit the final `skills/` directory against `design.md`. Verify the 12 skill directories exist with correct names, each has a `SKILL.md` with valid frontmatter, `skills/mission/` has `templates/` and `prompts/` subdirectories with all original files, and `skills/tdd/` has all 5 companion files. Flag any drift from the design.\n\n- [ ] C4. Documentation\n  Verify `README.md` accurately describes the post-refactor install and skill set. Verify `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` no longer describes test-quality as a \"separate skill\". Update any other in-repo documentation that references the old skill names or old install process.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQ7KMXY5J2GNHXG0357AGB7K","ts":"2026-04-27T13:57:13Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/*/spec.md; do printf '\\\\n## %s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,180p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"command_run","dispatch_id":"01KQ7KMXY5J2GNHXG0357AGB7K","ts":"2026-04-27T13:57:13Z","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/*/spec.md; do printf '\\\\n## %s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,180p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/*/spec.md; do printf '\\\\n## %s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,180p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"\n## openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/adversarial-review/spec.md\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: /adversarial skill exists\nA skill named `adversarial` SHALL exist at `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md` and be user-invokable.\n\n#### Scenario: Skill metadata is correct\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the frontmatter `name` is `adversarial`\n- **AND** `user-invokable` is `true`\n- **AND** the description mentions dual-agent review and Claude + Codex\n\n### Requirement: /adversarial accepts a review target\nThe skill SHALL accept an optional argument specifying what to review: a PR number, a file path, or no argument (defaults to current diff).\n\n#### Scenario: No argument reviews current diff\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` is invoked with no arguments\n- **THEN** the skill reviews uncommitted changes (`git diff` + `git diff --staged`)\n\n#### Scenario: PR number argument reviews PR diff\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial <number>` is invoked with a PR number\n- **THEN** the skill fetches the PR diff with `gh pr diff <number>` before spawning reviewers\n\n#### Scenario: File path argument reviews that file\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial <path>` is invoked with a file path\n- **THEN** the skill reads the specified file and uses it as the review target\n\n### Requirement: Two agents run concurrently\nThe skill SHALL spawn a Codex reviewer and a Claude reviewer in parallel so both complete in approximately the same wall time as the slower reviewer.\n\n#### Scenario: Codex reviewer dispatched async first\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` executes\n- **THEN** the Codex reviewer is dispatched via `darkfactory-dispatch --async` before the Claude reviewer is launched\n- **AND** the Claude reviewer is launched via the Agent tool after the Codex dispatch returns a job ID\n\n#### Scenario: Both reviewers receive identical input\n- **WHEN** both reviewers are spawned\n- **THEN** each receives the same review target content (diff or file)\n- **AND** each receives the same review instructions\n\n### Requirement: Reviewer prompts are adversarial and independent\nEach reviewer SHALL be instructed to review independently, without seeing the other's output.\n\n#### Scenario: Adversarial framing in prompts\n- **WHEN** each reviewer's prompt is inspected\n- **THEN** it instructs the reviewer to be independent and opinionated\n- **AND** it does not include the other reviewer's output or conclusions\n\n### Requirement: Findings grouped by severity\nEach reviewer's output SHALL group findings into severity levels.\n\n#### Scenario: Severity levels present\n- **WHEN** a reviewer produces output\n- **THEN** findings are grouped as: critical, warning, nit\n- **AND** each finding includes a `file:line` reference where applicable\n\n### Requirement: Reports written to files\nBoth reviewer reports SHALL be written to the local filesystem.\n\n#### Scenario: Codex report file\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` completes\n- **THEN** the Codex reviewer's report is written to `mission/validations/adversarial-codex.md` (or a temp path if run outside a mission)\n\n#### Scenario: Claude report file\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` completes\n- **THEN** the Claude reviewer's report is written to `mission/validations/adversarial-claude.md` (or a temp path if run outside a mission)\n\n### Requirement: Disagreements surfaced\nAfter both reports are collected, the skill SHALL identify and surface points where the two reviewers disagree.\n\n#### Scenario: Disagreements highlighted in summary\n- **WHEN** both reviewer reports are collected\n- **THEN** the skill presents a synthesis to the human that calls out findings mentioned by one reviewer but not the other, or findings where the severity assessment differs\n\n## openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/dispatch-skill/spec.md\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: /dispatch skill exists\nA skill named `dispatch` SHALL exist at `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` and be user-invokable.\n\n#### Scenario: Skill metadata is correct\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the frontmatter `name` is `dispatch`\n- **AND** `user-invokable` is `true`\n- **AND** the description mentions wrapping darkfactory-dispatch\n\n### Requirement: /dispatch accepts a task description\nThe skill SHALL accept a task description (from arguments or conversation context) and pass it to `darkfactory-dispatch` as the prompt.\n\n#### Scenario: Task from arguments\n- **WHEN** `/dispatch <task description>` is invoked with inline text\n- **THEN** the skill uses that text as the prompt passed to `darkfactory-dispatch`\n\n#### Scenario: Task from context\n- **WHEN** `/dispatch` is invoked with no arguments\n- **THEN** the skill asks the user for the task description before dispatching\n\n### Requirement: /dispatch calls darkfactory-dispatch with supervision\nThe skill SHALL invoke `darkfactory-dispatch` (not `codex exec` directly) so that timeout, heartbeat, and process group isolation are enforced.\n\n#### Scenario: Uses darkfactory-dispatch binary\n- **WHEN** `/dispatch` runs a task\n- **THEN** it calls `darkfactory-dispatch` with a prompt file and `--json` for structured output\n- **AND** it does not call `codex exec` directly\n\n### Requirement: /dispatch presents the result\nAfter the dispatch completes, the skill SHALL present the result to the user in a readable format.\n\n#### Scenario: Successful dispatch result shown\n- **WHEN** `darkfactory-dispatch` completes with status `completed`\n- **THEN** the skill prints the summary of what the worker did (from the structured JSON result)\n- **AND** it reports the duration and any files written\n\n#### Scenario: Failed dispatch result shown\n- **WHEN** `darkfactory-dispatch` completes with status `failed` or `timed_out`\n- **THEN** the skill reports the failure status and any error details from the result JSON\n- **AND** it does not suppress the failure\n\n### Requirement: /dispatch surfaces the output file path\nThe skill SHALL tell the user where the full output was written.\n\n#### Scenario: Output path reported\n- **WHEN** `/dispatch` completes\n- **THEN** the skill prints the path to the output file containing the full worker output\n\n## openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/install-script/spec.md\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: install.sh exists at repo root\nA POSIX-compatible shell script named `install.sh` SHALL exist at `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` and be executable.\n\n#### Scenario: Script is present and executable\n- **WHEN** a developer clones the Darkfactory repo\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` exists\n- **AND** the file is executable (`test -x ~/.darkfactory/install.sh` returns 0)\n- **AND** the script's shebang is `#!/bin/sh` (not `#!/bin/bash`)\n\n### Requirement: install.sh creates symlinks for all 12 skills\nRunning `install.sh` SHALL create a symlink in `~/.claude/skills/<name>` pointing to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each of the 12 skills.\n\n#### Scenario: All 12 skill symlinks created\n- **WHEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` is run on a clean machine (no existing symlinks)\n- **THEN** the following symlinks are created: `~/.claude/skills/mission`, `~/.claude/skills/grill`, `~/.claude/skills/language`, `~/.claude/skills/prd`, `~/.claude/skills/adversarial`, `~/.claude/skills/dispatch`, `~/.claude/skills/tdd`, `~/.claude/skills/test-quality`, `~/.claude/skills/security`, `~/.claude/skills/mission-resume`, `~/.claude/skills/mission-status`, `~/.claude/skills/mission-init`\n- **AND** each symlink resolves to its corresponding `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` directory\n\n### Requirement: install.sh is idempotent\nRunning `install.sh` a second time SHALL produce the same result without errors.\n\n#### Scenario: Re-run on existing symlinks\n- **WHEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` is run after it has already been run\n- **THEN** the script exits with code 0\n- **AND** all 12 symlinks still resolve correctly\n- **AND** no existing non-Darkfactory skills in `~/.claude/skills/` are modified or removed\n\n### Requirement: install.sh works on macOS and Linux\nThe script SHALL use only POSIX-portable constructs and work on both macOS (BSD coreutils) and Debian/Ubuntu (GNU coreutils).\n\n#### Scenario: Script uses no GNU-only flags\n- **WHEN** `install.sh` is reviewed\n- **THEN** it contains no `sed -i`, `date -d`, `stat -c`, `mktemp --suffix`, `readlink -f`, or `grep -P` calls\n- **AND** `ln -sf` is used to create symlinks (handles both creating and updating)\n\n### Requirement: install.sh reports what it did\nAfter running, the script SHALL print a summary of what was linked.\n\n#### Scenario: Successful install output\n- **WHEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` runs successfully\n- **THEN** it prints one line per skill symlink created or already-present\n- **AND** the final line reports the total number of skills installed\n- **AND** it exits with code 0\n\n### Requirement: README reflects the new install process and skill set\nThe README.md SHALL be updated to match the post-refactor structure.\n\n#### Scenario: Setup section replaced with install.sh\n- **WHEN** README.md is inspected\n- **THEN** the \"First-time install\" section shows `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` as the single install command\n- **AND** it contains no manual `ln -sf` commands for individual skills\n\n#### Scenario: Skills table uses current names\n- **WHEN** the README.md skills table is inspected\n- **THEN** it lists skills under their current names (e.g. `/mission-init`, `/mission-resume`, `/mission-status`)\n- **AND** it contains no legacy names (`/darkfactory-init`)\n\n#### Scenario: Required external skills section removed or updated\n- **WHEN** README.md is inspected\n- **THEN** the skills previously listed as \"required external\" from `layercodedev/skills` (`/grill-me`, `/ubiquitous-language`, `/write-a-prd`, `/tdd`, `/security-review`, `/test-quality-review`) are no longer described as external\n- **AND** they are either listed in the owned skills table or described as bundled\n- **AND** the only skills still marked as optional/project-specific are `/test-app` and `/demo-video`\n\n## openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/mission-orchestration/spec.md\n## MODIFIED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: scrutiny-validator.md references updated skill name\nThe scrutiny validator's check 14 (test quality review) SHALL invoke `/test-quality`, not `/test-quality-review`.\n\n#### Scenario: /test-quality-review reference replaced with /test-quality\n- **WHEN** `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` is inspected\n- **THEN** it contains no reference to `/test-quality-review`\n- **AND** check 14 references `/test-quality` wherever it invokes the test quality skill\n\n### Requirement: No other mission behavior changes\nThe mission SKILL.md SHALL remain otherwise unchanged: same phases, same rules, same 825-line monolithic structure.\n\n#### Scenario: Mission file is not internally decomposed\n- **WHEN** `skills/mission/SKILL.md` is inspected\n- **THEN** all phases (1 through 9) are present in the single file\n- **AND** the file does not delegate phases to separate skill files via sub-skill invocations\n\n### Requirement: Mission templates and prompts remain nested\nTemplate and prompt files SHALL stay under `skills/mission/templates/` and `skills/mission/prompts/` respectively.\n\n#### Scenario: Templates nested under skills/mission/\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission/templates/`\n- **THEN** all template files from the original `.claude/skills/mission/templates/` exist there\n\n#### Scenario: Prompts nested under skills/mission/\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission/prompts/`\n- **THEN** all prompt files from the original `.claude/skills/mission/prompts/` exist there\n\n## openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/setup-verification/spec.md\n## MODIFIED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init skill replaces /darkfactory-init with symlink verification\nThe `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md` skill SHALL check that `install.sh` has been run by verifying symlinks exist, instead of checking two separate source locations.\n\n#### Scenario: Symlink check replaces dual-location check\n- **WHEN** `/init` runs its skill checks\n- **THEN** it verifies that `~/.claude/skills/<name>` is a symlink pointing to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each of the 12 owned skills\n- **AND** it does not check `.claude/skills/` inside the repo or `~/.darkfactory-skills/` as alternate install locations\n\n#### Scenario: Broken symlink detected and reported\n- **WHEN** a skill symlink exists in `~/.claude/skills/` but does not resolve (dangling symlink)\n- **THEN** `/init` reports it as broken with the expected target path\n- **AND** it suggests running `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` to fix it\n\n#### Scenario: Missing symlink detected and reported\n- **WHEN** a skill is not symlinked (symlink absent entirely)\n- **THEN** `/init` reports it as missing\n- **AND** it suggests running `~/.darkfactory/install.sh`\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init reports all 12 expected skills\nThe skill SHALL check for all 12 skills by their current names.\n\n#### Scenario: Skill list is correct\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` checks skills\n- **THEN** the checklist includes: `mission`, `grill`, `language`, `prd`, `adversarial`, `dispatch`, `tdd`, `test-quality`, `security`, `mission-resume`, `mission-status`, `mission-init`\n- **AND** the checklist does NOT include: `grill-me`, `write-a-prd`, `ubiquitous-language`, `darkfactory-init`, `test-quality-review`\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init still verifies CLI tools\nThe skill SHALL still check for required CLI tools as before.\n\n#### Scenario: CLI tools checked\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs\n- **THEN** it checks for `codex`, `darkfactory-dispatch`, `gh`, `openspec`, and `jq`\n- **AND** for each, it reports whether it is installed and authenticated (where applicable)\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init reports install instructions when setup is incomplete\nIf any symlinks are missing, the skill SHALL print a single command to fix everything.\n\n#### Scenario: Install command shown on failure\n- **WHEN** one or more skill symlinks are missing or broken\n- **THEN** `/mission-init` prints: `Run: ~/.darkfactory/install.sh`\n- **AND** it exits after showing the report (does not attempt to create symlinks itself)\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init verifies coverage tool per detected language\nThe skill SHALL detect the project language from build files and check the appropriate coverage tool is installed.\n\n#### Scenario: Coverage tool checked for Rust project\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with `Cargo.toml` at the root\n- **THEN** it checks whether `cargo-tarpaulin` is installed\n- **AND** reports `[x] cargo-tarpaulin` if installed, or `[ ] cargo-tarpaulin (install: cargo install cargo-tarpaulin)` if not\n\n#### Scenario: Coverage tool checked for TypeScript/Node project\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with `package.json` at the root\n- **THEN** it checks `package.json` `dependencies` and `devDependencies` for `c8`, `@jest/coverage`, `istanbul`, or `jest`\n- **AND** reports the found package (e.g. `[x] jest (built-in coverage)`) or `[ ] no coverage package found (install: npm install -D c8)` if none found\n\n#### Scenario: Coverage tool checked for Python project\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with `pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt` at the root\n- **THEN** it checks whether `pytest-cov` is installed\n- **AND** reports `[x] pytest-cov` if installed, or `[ ] pytest-cov (install: pip install pytest-cov)` if not\n\n#### Scenario: No recognized language detected\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with no `Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`, or `requirements.txt` at the root\n- **THEN** it reports \"No recognized language detected -- coverage tool check skipped\"\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init still initializes OpenSpec if not initialized\nThe skill SHALL still run `openspec init` if `openspec/config.yaml` does not exist in the current directory.\n\n#### Scenario: OpenSpec init on first run\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory without `openspec/config.yaml`\n- **THEN** it runs `openspec init --tools claude,codex --force`\n- **AND** it reports \"OpenSpec: initialized\"\n\n## openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/skill-layout/spec.md\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Skills directory at repo root\nAll skills SHALL live in `skills/` at the Darkfactory repo root (`~/.darkfactory/skills/`), not in `.claude/skills/`.\n\n#### Scenario: skills/ directory exists with correct structure\n- **WHEN** a developer clones the Darkfactory repo\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/skills/` exists and contains exactly 12 subdirectories: `mission`, `grill`, `language`, `prd`, `adversarial`, `dispatch`, `tdd`, `test-quality`, `security`, `mission-resume`, `mission-status`, `mission-init`\n- **AND** each subdirectory contains a `SKILL.md` file with valid frontmatter (name, description, user-invokable fields)\n\n### Requirement: Legacy .claude/skills/ removed\nThe `.claude/skills/` directory inside the Darkfactory repo SHALL be deleted.\n\n#### Scenario: No .claude/skills/ in repo\n- **WHEN** the migration is complete\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/.claude/skills/` does not exist\n- **AND** `git ls-files .claude/skills/` returns no output\n\n### Requirement: .codex/skills/ duplicates removed\nThe `.codex/skills/` directory inside the Darkfactory repo SHALL be deleted.\n\n#### Scenario: No .codex/skills/ in repo\n- **WHEN** the migration is complete\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/.codex/skills/` does not exist\n- **AND** `git ls-files .codex/skills/` returns no output\n\n### Requirement: Forked skills present and self-contained\nSix externally-sourced skills SHALL be forked into the repo as owned files, not symlinks.\n\n#### Scenario: grill skill forked from grill-me\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/grill/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `grill`\n- **AND** the skill content matches the behavior of the original `grill-me` skill\n\n#### Scenario: prd skill forked from write-a-prd\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/prd/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `prd`\n\n#### Scenario: language skill forked from ubiquitous-language\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/language/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `language`\n\n#### Scenario: tdd skill forked with companion files\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/tdd/`\n- **THEN** `SKILL.md` exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** all 5 companion files exist: `deep-modules.md`, `interface-design.md`, `mocking.md`, `refactoring.md`, `tests.md`\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `tdd`\n\n#### Scenario: test-quality skill forked from test-quality-review\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `test-quality`\n- **AND** the skill content matches the behavior of the original `test-quality-review` skill (except the frontmatter name field)\n\n#### Scenario: security skill forked from security-review\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/security/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `security`\n- **AND** the skill contains no references to toyo-review or toyo-specific review sections\n\n### Requirement: Mission-family skills moved to skills/\nThree existing skills SHALL be moved to `skills/`. Two are moved unchanged; one is renamed.\n\n#### Scenario: mission-resume skill moved\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission-resume/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists with frontmatter name `mission-resume`\n- **AND** the skill content is identical to the original `.claude/skills/mission-resume/SKILL.md`\n\n#### Scenario: mission-status skill moved\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission-status/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists with frontmatter name `mission-status`\n\n#### Scenario: mission-init skill renamed from darkfactory-init\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists with frontmatter name `mission-init`\n\n### Requirement: Mission skill preserved with updated references\nThe existing mission SKILL.md and its companion files SHALL be moved to `skills/mission/`.\n\n#### Scenario: mission skill and companions moved\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission/`\n- **THEN** `SKILL.md` exists\n- **AND** `templates/` subdirectory exists with all original template files\n- **AND** `prompts/` subdirectory exists with all original prompt files\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
