{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md skills/mission/templates/plan.md openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/tasks.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/tasks.md b/openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/tasks.md\nindex a774424..8c86d51 100644\n--- a/openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/tasks.md\n+++ b/openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/tasks.md\n@@ -2,34 +2,34 @@\n \n ## Feature Tasks\n \n-- [ ] 1. Move mission skill, mission-resume, and mission-status\n+- [x] 1. Move mission skill, mission-resume, and mission-status\n   Move `.claude/skills/mission/` (SKILL.md + templates/ + prompts/) to `skills/mission/`. Move `.claude/skills/mission-resume/` to `skills/mission-resume/`. Move `.claude/skills/mission-status/` to `skills/mission-status/`. Do not change any skill content in any of these three.\n \n-- [ ] 1a. Update mission SKILL.md skill references\n+- [x] 1a. Update mission SKILL.md skill references\n   In `skills/mission/SKILL.md`, replace all occurrences of old skill invocation names with new ones: `/grill-me` → `/grill`, `/write-a-prd` → `/prd`, `/ubiquitous-language` → `/language`, `/darkfactory-init` → `/mission-init`. No other content changes. This implements PRD user story 10 and was added during the coverage audit.\n \n-- [ ] 2. Fork grill, language, and prd skills\n+- [x] 2. Fork grill, language, and prd skills\n   Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/grill-me/SKILL.md` to `skills/grill/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `grill`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/ubiquitous-language/SKILL.md` to `skills/language/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `language`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/write-a-prd/SKILL.md` to `skills/prd/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `prd`. Content otherwise unchanged.\n \n-- [ ] 3. Fork tdd and test-quality skills\n+- [x] 3. Fork tdd and test-quality skills\n   Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/tdd/SKILL.md` and all 5 companion files (`deep-modules.md`, `interface-design.md`, `mocking.md`, `refactoring.md`, `tests.md`) to `skills/tdd/`, update frontmatter name to `tdd`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/test-quality-review/SKILL.md` to `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `test-quality`. Also update the one reference in `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md`: replace `/test-quality-review` with `/test-quality` in check 14.\n \n-- [ ] 4. Fork security skill\n+- [x] 4. Fork security skill\n   Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/security-review/SKILL.md` to `skills/security/SKILL.md`. Update frontmatter name to `security`. Remove any toyo-review-specific sections (references to toyo's review conventions or toyo-specific severity levels). Preserve all general security review logic.\n \n-- [ ] 5. Write mission-init skill\n+- [x] 5. Write mission-init skill\n   Write `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md`. This replaces `darkfactory-init` with symlink-based verification. The skill checks that each of the 12 skills has a symlink at `~/.claude/skills/<name>` pointing to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>`. On missing or broken symlinks it suggests running `install.sh`. Retains: CLI tool checks (codex, darkfactory-dispatch, gh, openspec, jq), coverage tool detection per project language (Rust/TypeScript/Python), and `openspec init --tools claude,codex --force` if `openspec/config.yaml` is absent.\n \n-- [ ] 6. Write adversarial skill\n+- [x] 6. Write adversarial skill\n   Write `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md`. Standalone dual-agent review skill: dispatches a Codex reviewer via `darkfactory-dispatch --async`, then launches a Claude reviewer via the Agent tool. Both receive identical input (current diff by default; PR diff via `gh pr diff <number>` if a PR number is given; a specific file if a path is given). Reports written to `mission/validations/adversarial-codex.md` and `adversarial-claude.md` (or temp paths outside a mission). After both complete, surfaces disagreements between the two reports.\n \n-- [ ] 7. Write dispatch skill\n+- [x] 7. Write dispatch skill\n   Write `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md`. Thin user-facing wrapper around the `darkfactory-dispatch` binary. Accepts a task description inline or prompts for one. Calls `darkfactory-dispatch` with a prompt file and `--json`, parses the structured result, and presents outcome (status, duration, files written, output path). Reports failure clearly; does not suppress it.\n \n-- [ ] 8. Create install.sh\n+- [x] 8. Create install.sh\n   Write `install.sh` at the repo root. POSIX-portable (`#!/bin/sh`), loops over `skills/*/` directories, creates `ln -sf` symlinks from `~/.claude/skills/<name>` to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each. Idempotent. Prints one line per skill and a final count. Make the file executable.\n \n-- [ ] 9. Update README.md and UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- [x] 9. Update README.md and UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n   Rewrite three README sections: (1) First-time install — replace the block of manual `ln -sf` commands with `git clone` + `~/.darkfactory/install.sh`. (2) Skills table — replace the 4-row legacy table with the full 12-skill table. (3) Required external skills section — skills previously listed as external (`grill-me`, `ubiquitous-language`, `write-a-prd`, `tdd`, `test-quality-review`, `security-review`) are now bundled; remove them from the external table, keep only `/review` and `/simplify` (built-in Claude Code) and `/test-app` and `/demo-video` (optional project-specific). Update UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md: change \"separate skill\" to \"owned skill\" in the test-quality term definition.\n \n ## Closing Tasks\n@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@\n - [ ] C1. Smoke test\n   Run `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` and verify: (1) all 12 symlinks exist under `~/.claude/skills/` and resolve to the correct `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` targets; (2) running `/mission-init` in a project with a `Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, or `pyproject.toml` reports the expected coverage tool status.\n \n-- [ ] C2. Cleanup\n+- [x] C2. Cleanup\n   Remove any dead code, leftover scaffold, or draft files introduced during the mission. Check that no skill file contains references to old names (`grill-me`, `write-a-prd`, `ubiquitous-language`, `darkfactory-init`, `test-quality-review`). Verify no skill references the external `~/.darkfactory-skills/` repo path.\n \n - [ ] C3. Module shape re-check\ndiff --git a/skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md b/skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md\nindex 3624271..c1ee729 100644\n--- a/skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md\n+++ b/skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md\n@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@ Run these checks in order. For each, report PASS or FAIL with evidence.\n \n 8. **Code simplify:** Run /simplify against the changed files. \n \n-9. **Security review:** If the diff touches auth, secrets, user input, network boundaries, or filesystem trust boundaries (copying/moving/promoting files between directories, extracting archives, sandbox-to-production transfers), run /security-review. Otherwise \"N/A.\"\n+9. **Security review:** If the diff touches auth, secrets, user input, network boundaries, or filesystem trust boundaries (copying/moving/promoting files between directories, extracting archives, sandbox-to-production transfers), run /security. Otherwise \"N/A.\"\n \n 10. **Contract assertions:** Mark each assertion PASS, FAIL, or SKIP with a one-line explanation. SKIPs for work deferred to later tasks: append to `mission/deferrals.md` as `task N -- <assertion>`.\n \n@@ -243,9 +243,9 @@ Run these checks in order. For each, report PASS or FAIL with evidence.\n \n     Report success as `diff-coverage | PASS | 85% coverage on changed lines`. Report warnings as `diff-coverage | WARN | 74% coverage on changed lines (target: 80%)`. Report failures as `diff-coverage | FAIL | 55% coverage on changed lines (minimum: 70%)`. Include details listing under-covered files with added-line ranges that lack coverage.\n \n-14. **Test quality review:** If the diff contains no test files, report `test-quality-review | SKIP | no test files in diff`.\n+14. **Test quality review:** If the diff contains no test files, report `test-quality | SKIP | no test files in diff`.\n \n-    Run /test-quality as a subagent against the full diff, following the same delegation pattern as /review, /simplify, and /security-review. Read the skill markdown findings after the subagent completes. Findings are grouped by severity (P0, P1, P2, P3) and include file:line, evidence, and remediation.\n+    Run /test-quality as a subagent against the full diff, following the same delegation pattern as /review, /simplify, and /security. Read the skill markdown findings after the subagent completes. Findings are grouped by severity (P0, P1, P2, P3) and include file:line, evidence, and remediation.\n \n     Apply this severity-based result behavior:\n     - Any P0 finding, including tautological assertions, is a FAIL.\n@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@ Run these checks in order. For each, report PASS or FAIL with evidence.\n     - P2 and P3 findings only are WARNINGS; include them in the report but do not fail the task.\n     - No findings is PASS.\n \n-    Report passing output as `test-quality-review | PASS | no findings`. Report warning output as `test-quality-review | WARN | 2 P2, 1 P3 findings`. Report failing output as `test-quality-review | FAIL | 1 P0 finding (tautological assertion in test_list_open)`. Include a summary of findings in the notes column.\n+    Report passing output as `test-quality | PASS | no findings`. Report warning output as `test-quality | WARN | 2 P2, 1 P3 findings`. Report failing output as `test-quality | FAIL | 1 P0 finding (tautological assertion in test_list_open)`. Include a summary of findings in the notes column.\n \n ## Output Format\n \ndiff --git a/skills/mission/templates/plan.md b/skills/mission/templates/plan.md\nindex d73dcc1..a1bc45e 100644\n--- a/skills/mission/templates/plan.md\n+++ b/skills/mission/templates/plan.md\n@@ -28,13 +28,13 @@ Captured so this mission can be reproduced against the exact skill version that\n Defaults defined in Phase 6 config.yaml. \n \n ## Skills to Use\n-- /grill-me -- alignment interview (planning)\n-- /ubiquitous-language -- shared language (planning)\n-- /write-a-prd -- structured PRD from grill conversation (planning)\n+- /grill -- alignment interview (planning)\n+- /language -- shared language (planning)\n+- /prd -- structured PRD from grill conversation (planning)\n - openspec CLI -- create artifacts sequentially: proposal, specs, design, tasks (planning)\n - /review -- code review (scrutiny validation)\n - /simplify -- simplify pass (scrutiny validation)\n-- /security-review -- security check (scrutiny validation, sensitive tasks only)\n+- /security -- security check (scrutiny validation, sensitive tasks only)\n - /tdd -- test-driven development for workers (build phase)\n - /test-app -- browser tests (user-test validation)\n - /demo-video -- frontend demo recording (post-validation)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
